@attribute [Route(GuestSignInRegistration.SignInPath)]
@using NFHotel.Web.Security
@inherits NFHotel.Web.Common.CancellableComponentBase

@inject GuestSignInViewModel ViewModel
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@*
    The guest sign-in (MIL-018, ADR-0049, UC-010): the booking reference and the email the booking was made with sign
    the guest in to that booking, and the guest's own page /my-booking shows it, with the dates to change and the button
    to cancel. The reference is random (ADR-0049 decision 1), so it cannot be worked out from another booking; the page
    reads nothing in it and sends it to the API as typed, which decides and counts every try.

    A static server-rendered form, with no @@rendermode: the guest cookie can only be set while the response is being
    made, and a SignalR circuit cannot set one. The cookie is a scheme of its own, beside the staff cookie, so a guest is
    never taken for a member of staff (ADR-0047 decision 6).

    Neither the reference nor the email goes in the address: the form sends both in the body, so they stay out of access
    logs and the browser history. An old link with a booking number (/booking/FLZ-000123) is sent to this page empty
    (GuestSignInRegistration.MapGuestSession).

    PublicLayout is the default layout (Routes.razor), so there is no @@layout line.
*@

<PageTitle>Find your booking — NFHotel</PageTitle>

<div class="pub-section">
    <div class="pub-wrap">
        <div class="pub-booking stack-lg">
            <PageHeader Title="Find your booking"
                        Subtitle="Enter your booking reference and the email you booked with." />

            <ErrorAlert Errors="ViewModel.Errors" />

            @* Input is set in OnInitialized, before the first render, so it is never null where the fields bind to it. *@
            <EditForm Model="Input" FormName="@FormName" OnValidSubmit="SignInAsync" method="post" class="card card-pad stack">
                <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                <div class="field-row">
                    <FormField Label="Booking reference" For="booking-reference" IsRequired="true"
                               Hint="It is on your confirmation: letters and digits in five groups.">
                        <InputText id="booking-reference" class="field-input pub-reference-input" autocomplete="off"
                                   spellcheck="false" maxlength="@BookingReference.TextLength" @bind-Value="Input!.Reference" />
                    </FormField>

                    <FormField Label="Email" For="booking-email" IsRequired="true"
                               Hint="The email you booked with.">
                        <InputText id="booking-email" type="email" class="field-input" autocomplete="email"
                                   maxlength="@Guest.MaxEmailLength" @bind-Value="Input!.Email" />
                    </FormField>
                </div>

                <ValidationSummary />

                <div class="row">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Show my booking</button>
                </div>
            </EditForm>

            <p class="muted">
                If it still doesn't work, email help@nfhotel.com and reception will find the booking for you.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
